# Jobseeker API URL conventions

## Prefix

All JobseekerModule backend routes live under **`/api/jobseekers/`** (module root). Do **not** add a redundant `jobseeker` segment (`/api/jobseekers/jobseeker/…`).

| Area | Base path |
|------|-----------|
| Profile completion tabs | `/api/jobseekers/profile-completion/` |
| General info + work scope | `/api/jobseekers/profile/` |
| Admin / operator | `/api/jobseekers/admin/…` |

## Profile id — token only (self-service routes)

For routes that mutate or list **the logged-in job seeker’s own data**, never put `{profileId}` in the URL.

```csharp
[Authorize]
[HttpDelete("experiences/{id:int}")]
public async Task<IActionResult> DeleteExperience(int id)
{
    var profileId = int.Parse(CommonAction.GetLoggedInUserProfileId(User));
    // ...
}
```

- Frontend calls `/api/jobseekers/profile-completion/experiences/2`, not `…/experiences/2519/2`.
- NgRx may still key cache by `profileId` from `auth/me`; that stays in app state, not the HTTP path.

## When profile id in URL is OK

Keep `{profileId}` only when the caller is **not** scoped to self — e.g. operator/admin reading another user (`/api/v2/auth/profiles/{id}/summary`, admin company verify, interview documents for a candidate pair).

## Examples

```text
✅ GET  /api/jobseekers/profile-completion/experiences
✅ DELETE /api/jobseekers/profile-completion/experiences/2
✅ GET  /api/jobseekers/profile/general-info
❌ DELETE /api/jobseekers/jobseeker/experiences/2519/2
❌ GET  /api/jobseekers/profile/general-info/2519
```
